    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-18244: the minor is 2k(k+3)-66; setting it to -70 gives (k+1)(k+2)=0. q-13759: every entry above the diagonal is zero, while entries below it are nonzero, so the matrix is lower triangular. q-68710: every off-diagonal entry is zero, making diagonal the most specific description. q-74316: only B has all entries above the diagonal zero. q-42090: A has all entries below the diagonal zero; B and C fail because b31=5 and c32=3. q-74319: D is lower triangular but not upper triangular, and its transpose is upper triangular, so II and III hold. q-13771: A and its transpose are diagonal; their sum is diagonal as well, so all three statements hold. q-38176: expansion along the second row gives 2(6(-1)-7(1))=-26. q-77477: det(S)=1+2\\sqrt{3}, which is nonzero and different from \\sqrt{3}, so only I holds. q-38187: the third column is the negative of the first, so the determinant is zero and only II holds. q-18256: the determinant is -9y^2-34y+56; equating it to 81 yields (9y+25)(y+1)=0. q-128506: the determinant is m^2-12m+3; equating it to -29 yields (m-4)(m-8)=0. q-149766: the transformation gives a=-3, b=5, c=0.1, hence 2.1. q-111520: a=1, b=-2, c=1/4, hence -3/4. q-111563: 1≤Y≤3 corresponds to X=-2,0,2, whose probabilities sum to 1/12+5/12+1/4=3/4. q-149771: Y≤-6 is equivalent to X≥0, whose probabilities sum to 1/5+1/10+3/10=3/5. The current choice tokens below are taken directly from the supplied fields; confirmation rests on captured worked solutions, not on inferred grading.",
